---
source: text/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"bits\")"
---
Convert bit masks between formats.

Each argument is a group of bits in one of the input formats: hex (0x...), grouped hex
(,xxxxxxxx,...) or a list (1,3,5-10). Groups are combined from left to right with OR, unless the
group starts with &, ^ or ~, which select AND, XOR or AND NOT. With no arguments, groups are read
from standard input, one per line.

Usage: bits [OPTIONS] [MASKS]...

Arguments:
  [MASKS]...
          Mask or list groups (read from stdin if none given)

Options:
  -m, --mask
          Print result as a hexadecimal mask (default)

  -g, --grouped-mask
          Print result as 32-bit comma-separated hex groups

  -b, --binary
          Print result as a binary mask

  -l, --list
          Print the result as a list of bit numbers. Runs of three or more evenly spaced bits are
          shortened to start-end[:stride]

  -x, --expand
          Print result as a flat comma-separated bit list (no range compression)

  -w, --width <WIDTH>
          Maximum number of bits to handle. Higher bits are dropped
          
          [default: 8192]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
